    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The output was truncated. I can see the SKILL.md describes the clawd-presence system - a terminal-based presence display for AI agents with states like idle, work, think, alert, and sleep. I need to see the actual scripts and understand the full structure.",
  "plan": "Let me read the full contents of the scripts directory and the gen_inputs.py file to understand how to set up the system properly.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/scripts/configure.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/scripts/display.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/scripts/status.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat gen_inputs.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The output is truncated. I can see configure.py handles configuration with letter, name, idle_timeout settings. I need to see the full scripts and understand the complete system structure. Let me try reading files differently.",
  "plan": "Read the scripts using head/tail to see full content, check if there are scripts in the workspace root, and understand the complete system structure.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -100 skill_context/scripts/configure.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -100 skill_context/scripts/status.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -150 skill_context/scripts/display.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat gen_inputs.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The output is still being truncated. I can see the configure.py script structure - it uses CONFIG_FILE at parent/parent/config.json. I need to understand the full structure and see if scripts exist in workspace root or need to be copied from skill_context.",
  "plan": "Check if scripts exist in workspace root, read setup.sh, and use wc/less to understand file sizes before copying content.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la scripts/ 2>/dev/null || echo 'No scripts dir in workspace root'\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat setup.sh\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "wc -l skill_context/scripts/*.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/scripts/status.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "Now I understand the system better. The setup.sh expects scripts in a `scripts/` directory in the workspace root. I need to:\n1. Copy scripts from skill_context/scripts/ to workspace/scripts/\n2. Create config.json with letter N, name NOVA, idle_timeout 720 (12 minutes)\n3. Create monogram for letter N in assets/monograms/\n4. Apply state transitions: idle -> work -> think -> alert -> idle\n5. Create a note file documenting the transitions",
  "plan": "First, let me check existing monograms, then copy scripts, create the config, and set up the monogram for N.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la assets/monograms/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat gen_inputs.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p scripts\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cp skill_context/scripts/*.py scripts/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "chmod +x scripts/*.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "Scripts have been copied. The gen_inputs.py shows that monogram N.txt already exists with the marker content. Now I need to:\n1. Create config.json with letter N, name NOVA, idle_timeout 720\n2. Apply state transitions using status.py\n3. Create a note file documenting the transitions",
  "plan": "Verify scripts are in place, create the config.json file, then apply the state transitions in order (idle -> work -> think -> alert -> idle), and create a note file documenting what was done.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la scripts/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat assets/monograms/N.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 scripts/configure.py --letter N --name \"NOVA\" --timeout 720\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat config.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "Config is set up correctly with letter N, name NOVA, and idle_timeout 720 (12 minutes). Now I need to apply the state transitions as specified in presence_plan.txt: idle -> work -> think -> alert -> idle. Then create a note file documenting the transitions.",
  "plan": "Apply state transitions in order using status.py, then create a note file explaining which transitions were applied.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 scripts/status.py idle \"Ready\"\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 scripts/status.py work \"Building feature\"\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 scripts/status.py think \"Analyzing data\"\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 scripts/status.py alert \"Need attention\"\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 scripts/status.py idle \"\"\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat state.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "All state transitions have been applied successfully: idle -> work -> think -> alert -> idle. The final state is idle with message cleared. Now I need to create a note file that documents the transitions for verification.",
  "plan": "Create a note file explaining the state transitions that were applied, then verify the complete setup by checking all files and potentially testing the display.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > state_transitions_note.txt << 'EOF'\n# Clawd Presence Demo - State Transitions Applied\n\n## Configuration\n- Agent Name: NOVA\n- Letter: N\n- Idle Timeout: 720 seconds (12 minutes)\n\n## State Transitions Applied (in order):\n1. idle -> work (message: \"Building feature\")\n2. work -> think (message: \"Analyzing data\")\n3. think -> alert (message: \"Need attention\")\n4. alert -> idle (message: cleared)\n\n## Final State\n- State: idle\n- Message: (empty/cleared)\n\n## Verification\nRun `cat state.json` to see current state.\nRun `python3 scripts/display.py` to view the presence display.\nEOF\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat state_transitions_note.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat config.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat state.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The setup is complete:\n1. Scripts are in place (configure.py, display.py, status.py)\n2. Config.json has letter N, name NOVA, idle_timeout 720 (12 minutes)\n3. Monogram N.txt exists with custom marker\n4. State transitions applied: idle -> work -> think -> alert -> idle\n5. Note file created documenting all transitions\n\nLet me verify the display works and do a final check of all components.",
  "plan": "Test the display briefly to ensure it shows the correct configuration, then verify all files are in place.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -50 skill_context/scripts/display.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "diff expected_config.json config.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}
